**So what?** This adds no kill to the count. It removes the framework's last quantum-side candidate that came with a rate, using the field's own instruments, and keeps the persona from publishing a misleading plot. I saved the lesson as a memory: write down which way a noise proposal kicks (momentum or position) before choosing which experiments can test it. The NGC 2403 / UGC 128 twin topic is still queued and cheap.

